---
title: Desktop path — the live Ask loop, and the verifier loop nothing calls
---
%%{accTitle: "Desktop path as shipped: there is no intent classifier and no desktopAgent node. The model chooses one of the 32 desktop tools inside the single Ask-mode Agent that runAskTurn builds in src/main/services/pi/ask-turn.ts, which binds the desktop family through getDesktopToolbox() in pi/agent.ts. Tools never throw; they return isError plus details, and reach Win32 through koffi FFI, UIA through node-winautomation COM, and OCR through tesseract plus desktopCapturer, all behind WindowsDesktopAdapter. Cancellation is the chat pump's own AbortController: chat:cancelTurn aborts it, the listener calls agent.abort(), and withAbort settles the run even if the model never answers. The second box is the truth about the pixel verifier: PiDesktopAgent in pi/agent.ts owns the initial-screenshot decision, the details.verifies opt-in that runs GroundTruthVerifier, and the agent.steer() feedback, and it declares toolExecution parallel — but runPiDesktopTask() and abortPiDesktopRun() have zero production callers, so a shipped desktop turn runs the tools with no verifier in the loop. There is no approval gate anywhere: every tool runs without asking."}%%
